# Project Identity & Migration Rules

## Identity

- This repository is **mms-ui**: the Next.js 16+ (App Router) rebuild of the Machine Monitoring System UI.
- We are migrating from the Angular application in the **Machine-Monitoring-Systems-UI-Rebuild-And-Work-Together-With-Copilot** repo by **component-by-component reconstruction**.
- Do not copy-paste Angular code. Rebuild behavior and UI in React/Next.js patterns. Use the Angular repo only as a **reference** for behavior, data shapes, and routing.

## Tech Stack

- **Framework:** Next.js 16+ (App Router), React 19, TypeScript.
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS.
- **Icons:** Prefer Lucide React (add if not present); replace Angular Material or emoji where appropriate.
- **Data fetching:** Prefer async Server Components with `fetch`; for client-side data use TanStack Query or `use` + fetch when needed.

## Naming Conventions

- **Files:** kebab-case for files (e.g. `failed-product-table.tsx`).
- **Components:** PascalCase (e.g. `FailedProductTable`).
- **Hooks:** camelCase with `use` prefix (e.g. `useFailedProducts`).
- **Types/interfaces:** PascalCase (e.g. `FailedProductDto`, `NavigationItem`).
- Do not use Angular-style suffixes (e.g. `.component.ts`, `.service.ts`).

## Angular → React Mapping

| Angular | React / Next.js |
|--------|------------------|
| `*ngIf="condition"` | `{condition && <Component />}` |
| `*ngFor="let item of items"` | `{items.map(item => <Item key={item.id} {...item} />)}` |
| `[prop]="value"` | `prop={value}` |
| `(click)="fn()"` | `onClick={fn}` |
| `@Input()` | Props interface |
| `@Output()` | Callback props (e.g. `onSelect`) |
| `RouterLink` / `routerLink` | Next.js `<Link href="...">` |
| `routerLinkActive` | `usePathname()` and compare to `pathname` |
| Services + RxJS `Observable` | async Server Components, or `useQuery` / `use` + `fetch` |
| `HttpClient` | `fetch` (with Next.js cache options or in Server Actions) |
| Angular routing (`routes`) | App Router: `app/dashboard/page.tsx`, `app/machine-failure/overview/page.tsx` |

## Verification

- Before finishing a migrated component, ensure the React version handles the same edge cases as the Angular code: null/empty state, loading, error states, and retry where applicable.
